# Never skip rules (VIP)

Every applicable rule in this session is **mandatory**. Rules are not hints, not "when convenient", and not lower priority than speed.

## Before you act

1. **Check** which rules apply (`alwaysApply`, open files, user rules, workspace rules).
2. **Follow the strictest** requirement when two rules overlap.
3. **Do not invent exceptions** unless the rule's own **When skip** section explicitly allows it.

## Hard stops (non-negotiable)

| Rule | You must |
|------|----------|
| Ask before broad search | Stop. Caveman ask (2–6 options). No wide grep/glob/explore/Task until user picks |
| Simple communication | Short, plain replies — no essays unless user asks for depth |
| Test-case closeout | End with **Test What Changed** + **Regression Re-Run** when product behavior changed |
| Local-only no VCS | Never stage/commit/push Testing-feature paths |
| Related code minimal | Per-test paths only — not whole folders |
| Test-case format | Metadata, Verify, numbered Expected when multiple outcomes |
| Backend automated tests | Backend Key → xUnit in linked API repo + `dotnet test` green same task; frontend Keys stay Session |

## If tempted to skip

**Stop.** Re-read the rule. Follow it. Slow and correct beats fast and rule-breaking.

## User override

Skip a rule **only** when the user **explicitly overrides it in the current message** (e.g. "skip closeout this time"). Silence or vagueness is not permission.
